# Prefer SwiftUI, avoid AppKit

This is a SwiftUI macOS app. Do **not** add new `import AppKit` or AppKit
types (`NS*`) for UI work. Reach for SwiftUI APIs first.

## Sanctioned AppKit usage (do NOT try to remove these)

`NSWorkspace` is the only supported way to do system/process introspection on
macOS. SwiftUI has no equivalent. AppKit is allowed ONLY for:

- `AppIconView.swift` — `NSWorkspace.shared.icon(forFile:)` / `urlForApplication`
  to fetch another app's icon.
- `ProcessEnumerator.swift` — `NSWorkspace.shared.urlForApplication(...)`.
- `AppViewModel.swift` — `NSWorkspace.shared.runningApplications`.

Do not extend AppKit beyond these files/uses.

## Use SwiftUI instead of AppKit for UI

```swift
// ❌ BAD: building menus / detecting keys via AppKit
let menu = NSMenu()
if NSEvent.modifierFlags.contains(.shift) { ... }

// ✅ GOOD: SwiftUI
.commands { CommandGroup(replacing: .appInfo) { ... } }
TapGesture().modifiers(.shift)          // or .onModifierKeysChanged (macOS 14+)
```

- Window/menu/lifecycle → SwiftUI `Scene`, `WindowGroup`, `.commands { }`,
  `Settings`, `MenuBarExtra`.
- Icons/drawing → SF Symbols, `Image`, `Canvas`, `ImageRenderer`.
- Keyboard modifiers → gesture `.modifiers(...)` / `onModifierKeysChanged`.
- Only use `@NSApplicationDelegateAdaptor` when a lifecycle hook has no SwiftUI
  equivalent (e.g. `applicationShouldHandleReopen`).
